{"id":"NCT07157774","title":"Assessing the Impact of Muvalaplin on Major Cardiovascular Events in Adults With Elevated Lipoprotein(a)","official":"A Phase 3, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Study to Investigate the Effect of Muvalaplin on the Reduction of Major Adverse Cardiovascular Events in Adults With Elevated Lipoprotein(a) Who Have Had a Prior Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Event or Are at Risk for a First Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Event","summary":"The purpose of this study is to evaluate the efficacy of muvalaplin in reducing cardiovascular risk in participants with high lipoprotein(a) who have cardiovascular disease or are at risk of a heart attack or stroke.","conditions":["Elevated Lp(a)","Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease (ASCVD)"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Muvalaplin"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Have Lp(a) ≥175 nanomoles per liter (nmol/L)\n* Meet one of the following criteria:\n\n  * Have had a prior atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD) event (such as heart attack, stroke, or procedure to restore blood flow to the heart or other parts of the body) within 10 years prior to screening\n  * Are at risk for a first ASCVD event, defined as one or more of the following:\n\n    * Documented coronary artery disease (CAD), carotid stenosis, or peripheral artery disease (PAD) without a history of ASCVD event\n    * A high coronary artery calcium (CAC) score\n    * Reduced kidney function with diabetes\n    * Combination(s) of high risk factors\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Have experienced a major cardiovascular event or surgery, such as heart attack, stroke, or procedure to restore blood flow to the heart or other parts of the body, within 90 days prior to screening or occurring between screening and randomization\n* Are planning or expected to undergo a procedure to restore blood flow in the arteries or a major heart surgery during the study\n* Have uncontrolled high blood pressure\n* Have New York Heart Association (NYHA) class III or IV heart failure\n* Have undergone a procedure to remove cholesterol from the blood within 90 days of screening, or have a planned procedure during the study\n* Have severe kidney impairment\n* Have had cancer within 5 years prior to screening","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":10450,"start":"2025-09-02","pcd":"2031-03","upd":"2026-09-24","sponsor":"Eli Lilly and Company","areas":["other"],"central":["Trial questions or participation questions: 1-877-CTLILLY (1-877-285-4559) or · 1-317-615-4559 · LillyTrials@Lilly.com","Physicians interested in becoming principal investigators please contact · clinical_inquiry_hub@lilly.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Birmingham Clinical Research","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35209","s":"NYR","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"205-870-4343"},{"f":"Smiths Medical Center","city":"Apache Junction","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85120","s":"NYR","lat":33.4151,"lon":-111.5496,"c":"404-585-8358"},{"f":"Phoenix Medical Trials","city":"Gilbert","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85295","s":"NYR","lat":33.3528,"lon":-111.789,"c":"480-351-0755"},{"f":"Prime Medical Group, LLC dba Gilbert Center for Family Medicine, LLC","city":"Gilbert","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85296","s":"R","lat":33.3528,"lon":-111.789,"c":"480-691-2213"},{"f":"Onyx Clinical Research","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85014","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":"602-830-3794"},{"f":"Clinical Research Institute of Arizona (CRI) - Sun City West","city":"Sun City West","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85375","s":"R","lat":33.662,"lon":-112.3413,"c":"623-293-1360"},{"f":"Southwest Kidney Institute - Surprise","city":"Surprise","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85374","s":"R","lat":33.6306,"lon":-112.3332,"c":"480-610-6100"},{"f":"Pima Heart","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85741","s":"R","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":"5203149254 ex 13563"},{"f":"Eclipse 